	// RESULT-1: REFUTED (actual=5357.157549999999)

	// HYPOTHESIS-2: Lowering KV pressure threshold from 0.75 to 0.70 and using continuous scaling instead of step function will catch memory pressure earlier and reduce eviction-driven latency
	// MECHANISM-2: Continuous KV penalty (1-util)^2 provides smoother signal than step thresholds; earlier detection at 0.70 avoids routing to instances about to hit eviction cliffs
	// EXPECT-2: combined_score > -3900

